1eb4|n|A blank window or panel. ; A spherical body; a globe; especially, one of the celestial spheres; a sun, planet, or star. ; One of the azure transparent spheres conceived by the ancients to be inclosed one within another, and to carry the heavenly bodies in their revolutions. ; A circle; esp., a circle, or nearly circular orbit, described by the revolution of a heavenly body; an orbit. ; A period of time marked off by the revolution of a heavenly body. ; The eye, as luminous and spherical. ; A revolving circular body; a wheel. ; A sphere of action. ; Same as Mound, a ball or globe. See lst Mound. ; A body of soldiers drawn up in a circle, as for defense, esp. infantry to repel cavalry.	a:vbi,107,9;u5b,94,2;1ukr,91,3;28oj,47,2;7yj,44,4~vbi,107,9;7yj,44,4;1ukr,91,3;u5b,94,2;28oj,47,2	v:v40,100,2~v40,100,2	V:28at,122,5~28at,122,5	n:v40,110,4;u5b,104,4;1xig,26,3~v40,110,4;u5b,104,4;1xig,26,3	N:28ar,145,7;1wqx,97,5;28ax,44,4~28ar,145,7;1wqx,97,5;28ax,44,4
